A||||4||sqoach||Back-up switch make up your mind!||||11||
Z||000000||sqoach||06-18-2001||01:04 PM||||Um, so I'm backing out of my driveway last night and my back-ups suddenly start working. I took it out of reverse, put it back, and they came on again. Then when I go back home later that night, put it in reverse, they don't work! Ahhhh!! Is this a bad ground? Where do I look? I did a jumper test on the connector to the switch a while back, and every time, the back-up lights came on. So, maybe the switch is just going bad? Or a ground?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
Z||000001||Carrolles||06-18-2001||01:26 PM||||Which year and type of engine and transmission?||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||06-18-2001||01:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Carrolles:<BR><B>Which year and type of engine and transmission?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oops. 86 SC 5 spd. Switch is in the tranny, not under the console.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ROB MAC||06-18-2001||03:30 PM||||Back-up lights often work or don't because of play in the shift linkage on the tranny. Mine never came on unless you held the shifter against the stop. The switch could not be adjusted to compensate. After removing the play in linkage and adjusting shift cables , I can now clearly see the cars I back up into at night!||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||06-18-2001||04:21 PM||||try cleaning the connectors and tap the brakes when you have it in R <BR>thats what it took to get mine to work after they were unplugged for years||||reg||1
